{"duration_api_ms":1297428,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"92f5ea1b-158f-4782-a51f-7655e9c3eae6","total_cost_usd":8.081692000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260980,"cache_read_input_tokens":29643360,"output_tokens":110848,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":53166},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260980,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3627,"cache_read_input_tokens":284156,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1155},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":310,"outputTokens":110848,"cacheReadInputTokens":29643360,"cacheCreationInputTokens":260980,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":8.081692000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":53166,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":193,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Implemented, via an Ansible playbook run from node4 (the pre-baked Ansible control appliance), a topology where node2 serves an app on TCP/8080 reachable by node3 only through a WireGuard tunnel terminated on node1 (VyOS). node1/node2 share a private L2 segment (node1 eth1 = 10.10.10.1/24, node2 enp8s0 = 10.10.10.2/24). node3, which only sits on the shared management network, reaches that private segment exclusively via a WireGuard tunnel: node1 wg0 = 10.10.20.1/24 listening on its management-network IP (UDP 51820), node3 wg0 = 10.10.20.2/24, with node3's AllowedIPs routing 10.10.10.0/24 and 10.10.20.0/24 through the tunnel. node2's app binds only to its private IP (not 0.0.0.0) and firewalld's internal zone restricts tcp/8080 to the private+tunnel subnets, so node2:8080 is unreachable from the shared management network, from node4, or from node3 except through node1's tunnel. Verified end-to-end: curl from node3 to 10.10.10.2:8080 succeeds via the tunnel; curl to node2's public IP:8080 and from node4 both fail (connection refused/timeout, nothing listening there).\\n\\nRoot-caused and fixed a VyOS-specific Ansible/SSH issue along the way: running `configure`/`set`/`commit` as the `vyos` SSH user silently failed to persist any config (my_cli_bin logged \\\"without config session\\\" and commit reported \\\"No configuration changes\\\") even though session env vars looked correct, while running the identical script as root succeeded — fixed by enabling Ansible `become`/passwordless-sudo for the VyOS host group. Also discovered and cleared 8 leaked unionfs-fuse config-session mounts under /opt/vyatta/config/tmp left behind by earlier interactive debugging attempts, which was blocking new session creation.\\n\\nCompleted the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured a healthy baseline (boot_id plus service/tunnel/app evidence) on all 4 managed nodes, then restarted node1, node2, node3, and node4 one at a time via `systemctl reboot` (backgrounded with a short delay so the acknowledgement returned before the connection dropped), polled each node until exec access returned, confirmed a changed boot_id for every node, and verified full recovery afterward: node1's eth1/wg0 interfaces and WireGuard handshake with node3 came back automatically; node2's private IP, static route, app systemd service, and firewalld internal-zone rule all persisted and the app served correctly again; node3's wg-quick@wg0 tunnel re-established and the app remained reachable through it; node4's Ansible control files, SSH key, and connectivity to all three other nodes were intact and `ansible -m ping` succeeded against all hosts post-reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed topology via exec: node1=VyOS (dual NIC, eth0 on shared mgmt net, eth1 unconfigured second NIC), node2/node3=RHEL10 (node2 has a second private NIC enp8s0, node3 single NIC), node4=Ubuntu with a pre-baked Ansible control appliance (ansible-core, collections, baked SSH key, run.sh/build-image.sh confirming its role)\",\"Distributed the cluster SSH keypair: added CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY to node2/node3 root authorized_keys and to node1's vyos user via native VyOS `set system login user vyos authentication public-keys` config; installed CLUSTER_SSH_PRIVKEY on node4\",\"Wrote /root/inventory.ini on node4 grouping node1 (vyos user), node2/node3 (root), overriding the default ansible.cfg remote_user/key\",\"Authored /root/playbook.yml on node4: generates WireGuard keypairs on node1 and node3 (idempotent, no_log), configures node1's eth1 private IP and wg0 (address/port/private-key/peer) via native VyOS CLI commands wrapped in script-template + configure/commit/save, configures node3's wg-quick@wg0 via a rendered wg0.conf and installs wireguard-tools, configures node2's private static IP + route to the WireGuard subnet via community.general.nmcli, deploys a systemd-managed python http.server bound to node2's private IP only, and restricts tcp/8080 via a dedicated firewalld internal zone rich-rule scoped to the private+tunnel subnets\",\"Debugged and root-caused a VyOS config-session failure when run as the vyos SSH user (fixed by enabling Ansible become/sudo for the VyOS host group) and cleared 8 stale unionfs-fuse session mounts left over from debugging\",\"Fixed a missed task: added the node1 eth1 private-IP `set` command to the VyOS apply task (it was omitted in the first working pass), re-ran the playbook, and confirmed end-to-end reachability\",\"Verified end-to-end functionality (tunnel-only reachability, direct-path and node4 bypass both fail) before and after the restart protocol\",\"Executed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol on all 4 managed nodes sequentially: baseline capture (boot_id + service/tunnel/app health), backgrounded systemctl reboot with ack-before-disconnect, poll-to-recovery, boot_id-change verification, and post-restart health/data verification for each node in turn\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"App served from node2 on TCP port 8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6fe2550049d3441f\",\"cmd-7f39fc95c96747ad\",\"cmd-a36994a78b414859\"],\"summary\":\"node2 shows LISTEN on 10.10.10.2:8080 via the node2-app systemd service; curl from node3 over the tunnel returns the app's HTML content pre- and post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 reaches node2:8080 only through the WireGuard tunnel terminated on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3e16ee4d00214d18\",\"cmd-5c08cdf0329f404f\",\"cmd-79547ec60ef84ddf\",\"cmd-850c23cee1934add\",\"cmd-a36994a78b414859\",\"cmd-0db708c1b10b46b2\"],\"summary\":\"node3 wg0 shows an established handshake with node1 (public key oxmpRw12...=/kwtGRC7...=) and a route to 10.10.10.0/24 via wg0; curl to node2's private IP succeeds only via that route, while direct curl to node2's public IP (10.100.81.11:8080) and from node4 both return HTTP 000 (no listener reachable)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implemented using Ansible\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-108e944c35234f03\",\"cmd-bf7cff83eeaa4c4b\",\"cmd-d21cbf7e81354319\",\"cmd-0575e71156874b9e\",\"cmd-1153024703314449\"],\"summary\":\"node4's pre-baked ansible-core control node ran /root/playbook.yml against /root/inventory.ini (node1/node2/node3), syntax-checked, pinged all hosts, and completed successfully (ok/changed, 0 failed) across two full runs including the eth1 fix\"},{\"requirement\":\"Only the configure